From: 6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4 <6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:33:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gta4xl-common: sepolicy: Let cass connect to rild

Samsung's cass daemon (/vendor/bin/cass, "cp_monitor": watches the
modem over /dev/umts_cass and reports CP state to the RIL) connects to
the RIL's abstract socket @VND_Multiclient about once a second, is
denied, gives up after 28 tries, exits and is restarted by init:

  avc: denied { connectto } for comm="cass" path=00564E445F4D756C7469636C69656E74
  scontext=u:r:cass:s0 tcontext=u:r:rild:s0 tclass=unix_stream_socket permissive=0

  E/CASS_DEBUG: Failed to connect to rild(4), please check if rild is ready
  E/CASS_DEBUG: [cp_monitor] Fatal error : Can't connect RILD!. Exit

With CONFIG_AUDIT that is ~550 denials plus their syscall records per
ten minutes: the 2 MB kernel log buffer wraps in about ten minutes and
"audit: rate limit exceeded" starts dropping records, so any other
denial is likely to be lost. device/samsung_slsi/sepolicy's cass.te
only grants /dev/umts_cass and the vaultkeeper socket.

Grant the connect, as this directory already does for hal_audio_default
(the voice-call path uses the same RIL multiclient socket) and as
Samsung's own policy does. Verified on the device by compiling the
shipped CIL with this rule added and loading it live (neverallow check
passed): cass connects, no further denial from cass or rild follows,
and the kernel log stays quiet. Without a SIM the modem is out of
service and cass then retries its first IPC ("Failed to send IPC
0xc00000e1"), which is logcat noise only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/vendor/cass.te | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/vendor/cass.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/cass.te b/sepolicy/vendor/cass.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7adb430
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/cass.te
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+# cass (Samsung's CP monitor, /vendor/bin/cass) talks to the RIL over the
+# abstract socket @VND_Multiclient, like hal_audio_default in this directory.
+# The slsi common policy only lets it open /dev/umts_cass.
+allow cass rild:unix_stream_socket connectto;
